son vs verdict-r1.json)\n- The git sha (but I can't run git commands... but I need the git sha verified). Wait — \"verdict 必须写明 so 验证的 git sha\" — I need to write the git sha. But I'm forbidden from executing git commands. Hmm. Let me think. The git sha can be read from files (read-only). ci-results.json might contain the sha. Or state.json / run.json. Let me check. I can read files to find the sha. The base is f6f6057 per design. But \"so 验证的 git sha\" — \"so\" probably means the orchestrator / the verified git sha. Let me look for it in ci-results.json or other metadata.\n\nActually \"so\" might be a typo. Let me re-read: \"verdict 必须写明 so 验证的 git sha、通过数/总数、以及每条结论的证据\". Hmm, \"so 验证的 git sha\" might mean \"所验证的 git sha\" (the verified git sha). Probably means I should state the git sha that was verified. Since I can't run git, I'll need to find it from ci-results.json or state files.\n\nLet me first explore the task directory and find ci-results.json, plus check for existing review files.\n\nLet me do a broad exploration. I'll use the Agent Explore tool? Actually, the task is fairly bounded. Let me use Glob and Read directly. Let me look at the task directory structure first.\n\nLet me be careful: I should NOT execute git commands. But reading files is fine. Let me check what's in the task dir.\n\nLet me list files.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4-free","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b82503867dc9a59eebf43d351406","_messageId":"01a1b8251044710b8477e5d65b4e15fd","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b82503867dc9a59eebf43d351406","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b8251044710b8477e5d65b4e15fd","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b8251044710b8477e5d65b4e15fd","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a1b825-104